# Welcome — programmable notes

Noetic Journal is a **programmable note tree**: folders and pages you already understand, plus **purpose** (rules per note), **Lisp** macros, scheduled commands, and optional **document managers** when you enable AI on a note.

This page is a **short pitch** you can reuse in store listings and outreach. The full tour lives on [initial experience](noetic://document/initial%20experience).

## Day one

- Capture and organize notes in **collections** (diaries, checklists, projects).
- Run **macros** from the toolbar or speech.
- **Talk to a note** with **simple chat** (ask, tell, command)—without treating every note as an autonomous agent.
- Turn on **remote** or **local AI** when you want it ([Configure AI](noetic://document/Configure%20AI), [Configure local AI](noetic://document/Configure%20local%20AI)).

## Grows with you

- **Purpose** — how the note should behave and which tools are allowed.
- **Scripting** — same DLisp for macros, automation, and managers ([Scripting overview](noetic://document/Scripting%20overview)).
- **Optional discourse depth** — **context chat** (one note + `action-lisp`) and **Hi-IQ** (tree context, peer notes when purpose allows)—see [Document managers and collaboration](noetic://document/Document%20managers%20and%20collaboration).

## Why it feels different

| Typical “AI notes” | Noetic Journal |
| --- | --- |
| One global assistant | **Per-note purpose** and scripts |
| Opaque behavior | **Tool Catalog** + readable Lisp |
| Chat-first | **Notes-first** |
| Agent hype | **Your tree**, optional depth |

